{"call_id":"call_o2Xd9jXodFTkOsnUMDI5xzA6","process_id":"10576","turn_id":"019ca279-8025-7d00-ae3a-5b27c936e2a7","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","cd /workspace && kspec task get @01KJF68A"],"cwd":"/workspace","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJF68A"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"Session events: Add oversized payload guardrails with externalized blob pointers\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJF68AWM0F61QBQ957V6T2C1\nType:      bug\nStatus:    in_progress\nPriority:  1\nAutomation: eligible\nSession:   01KJH73C9JTMB6977AEY991KBQ\n\n─── Description ───\n  Problem: large ACP updates can inflate JSONL event lines and memory pressure. We need safety limits without losing auditability.\n  \n  Scope (steps 3-4):\n  1) Add framing/event safety caps (line/payload size) to prevent single-message heap blowups.\n  2) For oversized payload fields (toolResponse stdout/stderr, rawOutput, large chunk text), write full content to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/<id>/blobs/.\n  3) Store compact pointer objects in events.jsonl (path, bytes, sha256, truncated=true, preview).\n  4) Update session log show/search behavior to surface previews by default and optionally resolve blob content on demand.\n  \n  Non-goal: silently dropping payloads. If payload is externalized, events must keep enough metadata to reconstruct/audit.\nSpec ref:  @session-events\nTags:      session-log, memory, reliability\nCreated:   2026-02-27T09:18:10.836Z\nStarted:   2026-02-28T04:17:04.505Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nSession Event Storage\nType: feature\nImplementation: in_progress\nDescription:\n  JSONL-based event storage for agent sessions. Provides append-only event logs for auditability, session metadata tracking, and integration with kspec commit boundaries.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: a new session is started\n    When: createSession(id, metadata) is called\n    Then: creates .kspec/sessions/{id}/ directory with session.yaml metadata file\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: an active session\n    When: appendEvent(id, event) is called\n    Then: appends JSON line to events.jsonl with auto-assigned ts and seq\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: events are appended\n    When: written to disk\n    Then: uses atomic append (appendFileSync) for crash safety\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: a session exists\n    When: readEvents(id) is called\n    Then: returns all events in sequence order\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: session metadata\n    When: stored\n    Then: includes: task_id (optional), agent_type, status, started_at, ended_at\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: session ends\n    When: updateSessionStatus(id, status) is called\n    Then: updates metadata with status and ended_at timestamp\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: events are accumulated\n    When: a commit boundary is reached (task complete, session end)\n    Then: events are included in next kspec commit\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: A session event contains oversized payload fields (for example large tool outputs or chunk text)\n    When: The event is prepared for persistence\n    Then: Oversized field content is externalized to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/{id}/blobs/ and the JSONL event stores a pointer object instead of the full payload\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: Event payload content is externalized\n    When: The pointer object is written to events.jsonl\n    Then: The pointer records path, byte length, hash, truncation flag, and preview so audit trails remain reconstructible without silently dropping content\n\n─── Notes ───\n[2026-02-27T10:05:10.027Z] Jacob Chapel:\nStarted implementation. Adding session event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization + pointer metadata in store.ts, then wiring session log show/search to preview pointers by default with optional blob resolution flags and regression tests.\n[2026-02-27T10:09:39.744Z] Jacob Chapel:\nImplemented session event guardrails: appendEvent now externalizes oversized update.rawOutput, update._meta.claudeCode.toolResponse stdout/stderr, and chunk text into sessions/<id>/blobs with pointer metadata {path, bytes, sha256, truncated, preview}; added event-line cap fallback to externalize entire data payload if still oversized. Added pointer resolution utility and wired session log show/search with --resolve-blobs (default keeps preview pointers). Added regression coverage in tests/sessions.test.ts, tests/session-log-show.test.ts, tests/session-log-search.test.ts. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131). kspec validate still fails on pre-existing @observations slug ambiguity + baseline alignment/completeness warnings unrelated to this task.\n[2026-02-27T10:10:07.629Z] Jacob Chapel:\nSubmitted for review and opened PR #578 (fix/session-event-blob-guardrails). Includes event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization pointers and --resolve-blobs support in session log show/search with regression coverage. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131).\n[2026-02-28T04:15:59.721Z] @claude:\n[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: Missing AC annotation/test coverage for @session-events ac-7 (commit-boundary inclusion). Posted inline review comment on PR #578; requires follow-up before approval.\n[2026-02-28T04:18:29.579Z] @claude:\n[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Added explicit AC coverage for @session-events ac-7 with a new commit-boundary integration test in tests/sessions.test.ts. Test verifies accumulated session events are included in the next git commit by asserting sessions/<id>/events.jsonl appears in commit file list.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Session events: Add oversized payload guardrails with externalized blob pointers\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJF68AWM0F61QBQ957V6T2C1\nType:      bug\nStatus:    in_progress\nPriority:  1\nAutomation: eligible\nSession:   01KJH73C9JTMB6977AEY991KBQ\n\n─── Description ───\n  Problem: large ACP updates can inflate JSONL event lines and memory pressure. We need safety limits without losing auditability.\n  \n  Scope (steps 3-4):\n  1) Add framing/event safety caps (line/payload size) to prevent single-message heap blowups.\n  2) For oversized payload fields (toolResponse stdout/stderr, rawOutput, large chunk text), write full content to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/<id>/blobs/.\n  3) Store compact pointer objects in events.jsonl (path, bytes, sha256, truncated=true, preview).\n  4) Update session log show/search behavior to surface previews by default and optionally resolve blob content on demand.\n  \n  Non-goal: silently dropping payloads. If payload is externalized, events must keep enough metadata to reconstruct/audit.\nSpec ref:  @session-events\nTags:      session-log, memory, reliability\nCreated:   2026-02-27T09:18:10.836Z\nStarted:   2026-02-28T04:17:04.505Z\n\n─── Spec Context ───\nSession Event Storage\nType: feature\nImplementation: in_progress\nDescription:\n  JSONL-based event storage for agent sessions. Provides append-only event logs for auditability, session metadata tracking, and integration with kspec commit boundaries.\nAcceptance Criteria:\n  [ac-1]\n    Given: a new session is started\n    When: createSession(id, metadata) is called\n    Then: creates .kspec/sessions/{id}/ directory with session.yaml metadata file\n  [ac-2]\n    Given: an active session\n    When: appendEvent(id, event) is called\n    Then: appends JSON line to events.jsonl with auto-assigned ts and seq\n  [ac-3]\n    Given: events are appended\n    When: written to disk\n    Then: uses atomic append (appendFileSync) for crash safety\n  [ac-4]\n    Given: a session exists\n    When: readEvents(id) is called\n    Then: returns all events in sequence order\n  [ac-5]\n    Given: session metadata\n    When: stored\n    Then: includes: task_id (optional), agent_type, status, started_at, ended_at\n  [ac-6]\n    Given: session ends\n    When: updateSessionStatus(id, status) is called\n    Then: updates metadata with status and ended_at timestamp\n  [ac-7]\n    Given: events are accumulated\n    When: a commit boundary is reached (task complete, session end)\n    Then: events are included in next kspec commit\n  [ac-8]\n    Given: A session event contains oversized payload fields (for example large tool outputs or chunk text)\n    When: The event is prepared for persistence\n    Then: Oversized field content is externalized to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/{id}/blobs/ and the JSONL event stores a pointer object instead of the full payload\n  [ac-9]\n    Given: Event payload content is externalized\n    When: The pointer object is written to events.jsonl\n    Then: The pointer records path, byte length, hash, truncation flag, and preview so audit trails remain reconstructible without silently dropping content\n\n─── Notes ───\n[2026-02-27T10:05:10.027Z] Jacob Chapel:\nStarted implementation. Adding session event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization + pointer metadata in store.ts, then wiring session log show/search to preview pointers by default with optional blob resolution flags and regression tests.\n[2026-02-27T10:09:39.744Z] Jacob Chapel:\nImplemented session event guardrails: appendEvent now externalizes oversized update.rawOutput, update._meta.claudeCode.toolResponse stdout/stderr, and chunk text into sessions/<id>/blobs with pointer metadata {path, bytes, sha256, truncated, preview}; added event-line cap fallback to externalize entire data payload if still oversized. Added pointer resolution utility and wired session log show/search with --resolve-blobs (default keeps preview pointers). Added regression coverage in tests/sessions.test.ts, tests/session-log-show.test.ts, tests/session-log-search.test.ts. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131). kspec validate still fails on pre-existing @observations slug ambiguity + baseline alignment/completeness warnings unrelated to this task.\n[2026-02-27T10:10:07.629Z] Jacob Chapel:\nSubmitted for review and opened PR #578 (fix/session-event-blob-guardrails). Includes event payload/line guardrails with blob externalization pointers and --resolve-blobs support in session log show/search with regression coverage. Verification: npm run build; npx vitest run tests/sessions.test.ts tests/session-log-show.test.ts tests/session-log-search.test.ts (131/131).\n[2026-02-28T04:15:59.721Z] @claude:\n[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: Missing AC annotation/test coverage for @session-events ac-7 (commit-boundary inclusion). Posted inline review comment on PR #578; requires follow-up before approval.\n[2026-02-28T04:18:29.579Z] @claude:\n[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Added explicit AC coverage for @session-events ac-7 with a new commit-boundary integration test in tests/sessions.test.ts. Test verifies accumulated session events are included in the next git commit by asserting sessions/<id>/events.jsonl appears in commit file list.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":41271506},"formatted_output":"Session events: Add oversized payload guardrails with externalized blob pointers\n────────────────────────────────────────\nULID:      01KJF68AWM0F61QBQ957V6T2C1\nType:      bug\nStatus:    in_progress\nPriority:  1\nAutomation: eligible\nSession:   01KJH73C9JTMB6977AEY991KBQ\n\n─── Description ───\n  Problem: large ACP updates can inflate JSONL event lines and memory pressure. We need safety limits without losing auditability.\n  \n  Scope (steps 3-4):\n  1) Add framing/event safety caps (line/payload size) to prevent single-message heap blowups.\n  2) For oversized payload fields (toolResponse stdout/stderr, rawOutput, large chunk text), write full content to session blob files under .kspec/sessions/<id>/blobs/.\n  3) Store compact pointer objects in events.jsonl (path, by